From 401aa59b2a53a1f552b4c345be1062c784cae2d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:00:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: propagate resume errors before
 registration

Carry this reviewed SLIMbus/BAM change into maintained Linux 6.18.
Preserve the existing LTS channel-removal/reconfigure protocol, socket
interfaces and DMA provider implementation. This stage is exact patch.

The completed eighteen-change series passes 3,221 source-bound synthetic
cases and 117 independent regression controls, with normal LeakSanitizer
and fail-fast address/undefined-behavior sanitizers. These cover
startup, child and parent ownership, QMI allocation, TX completion
lifetime, synchronous/asynchronous response ownership, DMA admission and
the retained LTS stream caller. Baselines from the appropriate
intermediate stages fail their targeted assertions. All 108 ARM, ARM64
and ARM64 RT component objects build with W=1 and nonpermissive CFI
without diagnostics; their ELF source checksums match the final
candidate.

Kernel waits, workqueues, IDR, PM, packets, DMA and device services in
the host models are synthetic. No real firmware, audio, hardware,
network, phone or installed package executes. Full current-kernel link,
physical DMA-stop/recovery and final-image acceptance remain
unqualified. Codex prepared the LTS adaptations and qualification.
Preserve original authors, dates, notices and assistance credits. Human
DCO and owner, security and subsystem review remain pending; no new
sign-off is added.

Original reviewed changelog and provenance:

Runtime resume records a failed power-up state but always returns
success. Controller enable also ignores both the direct callback and PM
framework resume results. An initial QMI, DMA setup or capability
exchange failure can therefore expose a controller and consume its
bootstrap PM reference before hardware startup has succeeded. Registered
wake failures are hidden from their callers too.

Return the power-up error from runtime resume and check both resume
paths before registration. Unwind the new QMI client only for an
unregistered controller, retaining its bootstrap reference for retry or
removal. A failed wake of an already registered controller retains its
registration and existing client. Accept nonnegative PM framework
success, including its positive already-active result. Prepared DMA
resources retain their existing ownership for retry and normal teardown.

A host model composes 15 exact driver, core and PM callback bodies
against logical DMA, MMIO, QMI, completion and PM services. Each of two
PM profiles executes 626 cases: current PM passes 13284 checks after
2435 parent failures; the cached 6.18.63 PM callback passes 12708 after
2652 failures. The latter explicitly verifies hard-error latching and
blocked retry; it does not qualify an LTS backport or its recovery.
Twelve independent regression controls are rejected. Native ARM/ARM64
NGD/core objects build with LLVM21, W=1 and strict callback diagnostics
without warnings/errors.

Master-work and external-transfer quiescence, full failed-start
recovery, late QMI service handling and initial bootstrap remain
separate work. No real DMA, DMA callbacks, firmware, audio or phone
operations ran. Codex generated the fix, tests and changelog; human
review and DCO are pending.

Fixes: 917809e2280b ("slimbus: ngd: Add qcom SLIMBus NGD driver")
Fixes: 94fe5f2b45c4 ("silmbus: ngd: register controller after power up.")

Backported from commit 7cdceb93fcca ("slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: propagate
resume errors before registration")
---
 drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
index 534870bc88d01..ab6e72114e659 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -1422,7 +1422,7 @@ static int qcom_slim_ngd_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 		ctrl->state = QCOM_SLIM_NGD_CTRL_AWAKE;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_slim_ngd_enable(struct qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl *ctrl, bool enable)
@@ -1442,9 +1442,14 @@ static int qcom_slim_ngd_enable(struct qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl *ctrl, bool enable)
 		complete(&ctrl->qmi.qmi_comp);
 		if (!pm_runtime_enabled(ctrl->ctrl.dev) ||
 			 !pm_runtime_suspended(ctrl->ctrl.dev))
-			qcom_slim_ngd_runtime_resume(ctrl->ctrl.dev);
+			ret = qcom_slim_ngd_runtime_resume(ctrl->ctrl.dev);
 		else
-			pm_runtime_resume(ctrl->ctrl.dev);
+			ret = pm_runtime_resume(ctrl->ctrl.dev);
+		if (ret < 0) {
+			if (!ctrl->registered)
+				qcom_slim_qmi_exit(ctrl);
+			return ret;
+		}
 
 		if (ctrl->registered)
 			return 0;
-- 
